        {
          "id": 1075266873,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Right, so as long as `gcry_cipher_ctl()` is done before `gcry_cipher_authenticate()`, the part starting with line 4994 could be moved after the checks starting with line 5007-5048.\n\nPart of the problem why this was missed is that lines 5007-5048 already have checks that set the length of `aad_len`, and you can see on line 5042-5043 that there's a check for `else if (draft_version >= 25 || draft_version == 0) { aad_len = 5;`... but it wasn't added to this previous step.\n\nRather than have double logic, do 5007-5048 first, which sets `aad_len` then call `guint64 lengths[3] = { ciphertext_len, aad_len, auth_tag_len };  gcry_cipher_ctl(decoder->evp, GCRYCTL_SET_CCM_LENGTHS, lengths, sizeof(lengths))` without having to check the draft version / TLS 1.2 a second time.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
